<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis-Nicolas Davout</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1770">1770</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Marshal Davout</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis-Nicolas Davout (1770–1823) was one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s ablest marshals, victor over the Prussians at Auerstedt in 1806 and created Duke of Auerstedt and Prince of Eckmühl. As governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> in 1813–1814 he held the city against a Russian-led siege, expelling thousands of inhabitants and seizing the funds of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburger-bank">Hamburger Bank</a>. He surrendered it only after Napoleon's abdication.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-nicolas-davout.jpg" alt="Louis-Nicolas Davout" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: After Pierre-Claude Gautherot / Tito Marzocchi de Bellucci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Louis_nicolas_davout.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
